  "Rival Kazuo|When price reaches a goal, Dad watches bodies first, wicks second . Price needs a candle body (close) beyond the level to keep going. If it only pokes its nose (wick) past and fails to close, it will bounce back!": "3abe7a6323e8c7ed.mp3",
  "Rival Kazuo|Why do these matter so much? Because crowds of traders park their orders \u2014 and their stops \u2014 right around them. Lots of orders in one spot is called liquidity . Price gets pulled toward it like a magnet.": "b43f1912cb3703e2.mp3",
  "Rival Kazuo|Why so picky? Because breaking a fresh swing point proves strong buyers or sellers were really there. A gap that broke nothing new proved nothing. When price comes back to that one, do not expect it to hold.": "240bfb611919e4eb.mp3",
