  "|The candle closed, so NOW we act. We sell first right where it closed: 25,137.75.": "b61b67a816295aad.mp3",
  "|The candle trades through the level, taking the stops resting there, and the body closes back on the other side. That is a liquidity sweep.": "8e7b050ca048fa54.mp3",
  "|The central rule: take entries at your levels and take targets from your levels . Do not trade in the middle of the range between them.": "c47651cb47bfe8b5.mp3",
  "|The core course is done; the learning is not. This next part, the Strategy sections, replaces judgment calls made on feeling with exact rules .": "19c24a2ad2104444.mp3",
  "|The day divides into three sessions, named for which financial centre is open. First is Asia , roughly 6 PM to 3 AM Eastern . It is usually the quietest.": "83a9adc7f7be5fb6.mp3",
  "|The defense against all three is a trading plan . Before entering, decide: Why am I entering? Where is my stop-loss? Where will I take profit? Then follow the plan as written.": "eedbcecde061c9e1.mp3",
  "|The doji : almost no body, because the open and close are nearly equal. Neither side won. It signals indecision, and the following candle usually resolves it.": "7597dfbcd8b80b5a.mp3",
  "|The dojo rule is small: about 2 out of every 100 Koins you own. Let's work out what that actually is.": "33fac210154dcc07.mp3",
  "|The empty step runs from 40 at the bottom to 60 at the top. Halfway into it is which price?": "65ef619295b6f670.mp3",
  "|The equilibrium line: above it buyers feel strong, below it sellers rule.": "8f11298de602a52f.mp3",
  "|The failed break (a \u201cfailed-2\u201d): a candle trades beyond the previous candle's high or low but closes back inside. The attempt failed, and that failure is the signal.": "49c86b139d37a645.mp3",
  "|The final exercise combines everything so far: trade with the trend, use a stop-loss on every trade, and stay calm when the market gets fast.": "934c10be5d1da4f3.mp3",
  "|The final hour before the 4 PM closing bell, when the market wakes back up.": "75a3346b2b134b76.mp3",
  "|The first is FOMO , the fear of missing out. Price surges and you feel you must get in right now \u2014 often just before it pulls back. The disciplined response is to wait for the next proper setup.": "789b656463a76626.mp3",
  "|The flip. Once a ceiling truly breaks, the people who were selling there switch to buying there \u2014 so the same line now holds price up .": "e808eecdea9870fb.mp3",
  "|The grab and the snap-back. It went down to collect the shields, found no sellers left, and turned. That turn is the trade.": "1103f23508f3efb3.mp3",
